1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:05,780
Hello friends! Welcome to Tinku's Mahabharat!

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:12,445
I'm Tinku! And from today, we'll hear the biggest story in the world: the Mahabharat!

3
00:00:12,495 --> 00:00:17,710
It has kings, queens, brave warriors, and lots of good lessons too!

4
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,735
So come on, let's open the storybook!

5
00:00:22,235 --> 00:00:26,435
Long, long ago, there was a beautiful city called Hastinapur.

6
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:31,200
Its king was King Shantanu. He was very kind and fair.

7
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:35,665
My people's happiness is my greatest joy.

8
00:00:36,565 --> 00:00:40,745
One day, King Shantanu went for a walk by the river Ganga.

9
00:00:40,795 --> 00:00:43,745
Suddenly, a bright light rose from the water!

10
00:00:43,795 --> 00:00:47,220
And out of the river came a very beautiful goddess.

11
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:51,905
Who are you, goddess? I have never seen such radiance.

12
00:00:51,955 --> 00:00:55,525
I am Ganga, O king. The goddess of this very river.

13
00:00:55,575 --> 00:00:59,370
Will you become the queen of Hastinapur?

14
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:02,163
I will. But I have one condition.

15
00:01:02,213 --> 00:01:08,470
Whatever I do, you will never question me, and never stop me.

16
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:13,045
The day you stop me, that very day I will leave.

17
00:01:13,095 --> 00:01:17,870
I give you my word, goddess. I will never stop you.

18
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:23,410
And then, with a grand celebration, King Shantanu and Ganga were married!

19
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:27,790
Some time later, a little baby boy was born to them.

20
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:31,995
But Ganga took the baby to the river.

21
00:01:32,045 --> 00:01:36,535
And the baby rose into the sky, like a shining star!

22
00:01:36,635 --> 00:01:41,505
King Shantanu was shocked. But he had given his word, so he stayed silent.

23
00:01:41,605 --> 00:01:46,675
This happened not once, but seven times. One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!

24
00:01:47,175 --> 00:01:50,655
Friends, do you know who those babies were?

25
00:01:51,155 --> 00:01:56,925
They were the Vasus, gods of heaven! Because of a curse, they had to be born on earth.

26
00:01:56,975 --> 00:02:01,515
Mother Ganga was freeing them from the curse and sending them back to heaven.

27
00:02:02,415 --> 00:02:06,480
Then came the eighth baby. And Ganga walked towards the river once again.

28
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:11,910
Stop, Ganga! This time I won't stay silent! Give this child to me!

29
00:02:12,210 --> 00:02:15,467
O king, you have broken your promise.

30
00:02:15,517 --> 00:02:20,212
This is the eighth Vasu. He must live a long life on earth.

31
00:02:20,262 --> 00:02:25,876
Now I must go. But I will raise him, and bring him back to you.

32
00:02:25,976 --> 00:02:29,856
Ganga... my son... I will wait.

33
00:02:29,956 --> 00:02:34,116
And Mother Ganga, with the little baby, vanished into the river.

34
00:02:35,816 --> 00:02:40,936
Next time, see what that little baby grew up to be! A great warrior!

35
00:02:41,236 --> 00:02:45,106
Until then, goodbye friends! See you again!
